# Build products of `Scripts/`, and the generated Xcode project. None of these
# is source and none may be committed.
#
#   Frameworks/        the staticlibs `Scripts/build-core.sh` stages, per
#                      platform. They are ~10 MB artifacts of `core/`, and a
#                      committed copy is a copy that can be stale.
#   Sources/TwinVPNBridge/include/twinvpn.h
#                      the ABI OF RECORD, STAGED from core/ffi/include by
#                      `Scripts/stage-headers.sh`. README §2 and the module map
#                      both say why it is not committed: a second copy of an ABI
#                      of record is a second thing that can drift from it.
#   TwinVPN.xcodeproj/ generated by `xcodegen generate` from project.yml.
#                      §4 is the argument for why the spec is the source.
Frameworks/
Sources/TwinVPNBridge/include/twinvpn.h
TwinVPN.xcodeproj/
